{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 10 '\\\\*\\\\*D10|binding|protection' collab/1791194000000-architect-m-next-d-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | tail -35\nrg -n 'defn|frontier|prefix' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/input.cljc | tail -22\nsed -n '600,620p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"233-In `:exporting` and `:ended`, additionally: no child runs, a resume is refused, and each apply refuses a late result. A child created under a gated root has the root's mode and no custody map.\n--\n258:**D10.** Counter restored exactly; carried ids intact on the three variants; protection mismatch in each direction; a restored child does not rerun initialization; receiver-local store bindings do not change resolution.\n259-\n260-**D11.**\n261-- Assign before send; one increment; children draw from the root.\n262-- Retention across the four cases.\n263-- A reply failing any one of the five match fields discharges nothing.\n264-- A projected outcome of another incarnation is ignored.\n265-- A resent request after a regrant has a new request id and the same op id.\n266-- Unknown-effect transport error, cut before and after the commit.\n267-- After `:intent-conflict`: an at-least-once write is not performed, the release is carried, and the occurrence stays quarantined, open and ungranted.\n268-\n--\n283:- Each invalid binding answers `:yin.k/not-holder` and releases.\n284-- Unavailable ledger history never activates.\n285-- Renewal before half the duration; all IO stops at the bound.\n286-- **(residual 2)** After a post-grant failure the driver releases, and the occurrence is granted again to a candidate that proposes: an ordinary failed run stays regrantable. The driver itself proposes nothing on behalf of recovery.\n287-\n288-**D14.**\n289-- A crash at each intent and acknowledgment boundary reopens fenced with the same occurrence, waits and ids.\n290-- A crash between send and acknowledgment resends